sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant I as Interviewer
    participant C as Candidate
    participant N as The numbers
    I->>C: design it, and make it non-abstract
    C->>N: requests per second at peak
    C->>N: bytes per request, and per day
    N-->>C: storage and network footprint
    C->>N: work per request divided by what one machine does
    N-->>C: machine count, before replication
    C->>C: add failover headroom and a growth margin
    C->>I: here is the fleet, and here is the arithmetic
    I->>C: one rack fails
    C->>N: recompute with the survivors
    Note over C,N: NALSD means every box on the board has a number attached to it
